# Line endings, settled once.
#
# Without this file the repo pulled in two directions: `core.autocrlf=true`
# checks every text file out as CRLF, while `npm run format` (Prettier, whose
# `endOfLine` default is `lf`) rewrites every one of them back to LF. The
# result was a `git status` listing fifty-odd files that `git diff` reported as
# unchanged — the blobs were identical either way, so the noise was cosmetic,
# but it buried the real diff and read as "my change touched everything".
#
# `text=auto` keeps git's own rule: detect text, store it LF in the index,
# leave detected binaries alone. `eol=lf` is the half that was missing — it
# pins the WORKING TREE to LF as well, on every platform and regardless of a
# machine's autocrlf setting, so the checkout and Prettier finally agree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The binaries, marked rather than sniffed. text=auto already detects these
# correctly; saying so explicitly means a future file type can never be
# mangled by a mis-detection.
*.png binary
*.af binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp4 binary
